# Vulnerability details

## Impact
After incrementing a generation, the `generationMintCounts`is reset. This does not account for already generated NFTs by forging the previous generation. This contradicts the [whitepaper](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pihtkKyyxobFWdaNU4YfAy56Q7WIMbFJjSHUAfRm6BA/edit): "The game is capped at 10 Generations for now. Generations can only forge with each other and up to a max of 10000 for each generation.".

## Proof of Concept
After 10,000 NFTs are minted in one generation, `_incrementGeneration` is called. This resets the new generation [see](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-traitforge/blob/279b2887e3d38bc219a05d332cbcb0655b2dc644/contracts/TraitForgeNft/TraitForgeNft.sol#L345-L355).

To show this, [_tokenIds](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-traitforge/blob/279b2887e3d38bc219a05d332cbcb0655b2dc644/contracts/TraitForgeNft/TraitForgeNft.sol#L49) in TraitForgeNft must be changed to public.

Start by minting 10,000 NFTs. Also list and merge whenever possible:
```
while(nft.generationMintCounts(gen) < 10_000) {
  uint256 price = nft.calculateMintPrice();
  nft.mintToken{ value: price }(proof);

  uint256 tokenId = nft._tokenIds();

  uint256 entropy = nft.getTokenEntropy(tokenId);
  uint8 potential = uint8((entropy / 10) % 10);
  if (potential == 0) continue;

  if (nft.isForger(tokenId)) {
    nft.approve(address(forging), tokenId);
    forging.listForForging(tokenId, 0.01 ether);
    listedTokenIds.push(tokenId);
  } else if (listedTokenIds.length > 0) {
    nft.transferFrom(address(this), merger, tokenId);
    uint256 forgerId = listedTokenIds[listedTokenIds.length - 1];
    listedTokenIds.pop();

    vm.startPrank(merger);
    nft.approve(address(forging), tokenId);
    forging.forgeWithListed{value: 0.01 ether}(forgerId, tokenId);
    vm.stopPrank();
  }
}
```

Also print the current generation counts at the start:
  ________ start ____________
  gen:  1 0
  gen:  2 0

Print the current generation counts after minting 10,000 NFTs:
  ________ after minting 10,000 NTFs ____________
  gen:  1 10000
  gen:  2 2908

Print the current generation counts after incrementing the generation:
  ________ after incrementing generation ____________
  gen:  1 10000
  gen:  2 1

It can be seen that before increasing the generation, there are already 2908 gen 2 NFts (at this specific entropy). After increasing the generation by minting the first gen 2 NFT, the count gets reset to 1. Therefore there users can now mint up to 10,2908 NFTs of gen 2.

