## Impact
The [EntropyGenerator contract](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-traitforge/blob/main/contracts/EntropyGenerator/EntropyGenerator.sol) initializes entropy values using `keccak256` combined with `block.number` and an index. This method of entropy generation can be predictable to some extent by a potential exploiter. 

The predictability of entropy values can allow an attacker to create NFTs with specific desired traits, thereby compromising the fairness and randomness of the system.

## Proof of Concept
The contract generates entropy values in three batch functions: writeEntropyBatch1(), writeEntropyBatch2(), and writeEntropyBatch3().

```solidity
  // Functions to initalize entropy values inbatches to spread gas cost over multiple transcations
  function writeEntropyBatch1() public {
    require(lastInitializedIndex < batchSize1, 'Batch 1 already initialized.');

    uint256 endIndex = lastInitializedIndex + batchSize1; // calculate the end index for the batch
