A malicious actor can create unfillable forge listings by using a contract that reverts upon receiving ETH. When users attempt to forge their NFTs with these listings using the `EntityForging.forgeWithListed()` function, the transactions will fail, resulting in wasted gas fees and potential financial losses for the buyers.

If unfillable listings become widespread, they could significantly undermine user confidence in the protocol. Users may perceive the platform as unreliable, leading to decreased activity and a potential decline in core game metrics, e.g. player count, forging count etc.

